Article 35

Accompaniment Services as referred to in Article  28 paragraph (1) letter g, include:
a. 1) accompanying victims during the examination and health recovery process;

accompanying victims during the medicolegal process;  accompanying victims during the mediation process and/or examination at the Police, Prosecutor's Office, and Court;  monitoring the interests and rights of victims in the examination process at the Police, Prosecutor's Office and Court;  maintaining the privacy and confidentiality of victims from all parties who have no interest, including coverage by mass media;

coordinating with other companions; and  providing continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage.

Article 36

The provision of services to Victims as referred to in Article 28 is carried out every day (including holidays), in a manner that is:
a. fast;
b. safe and comfortable;
c. empathetic;
